  [PASS] P0-d0 CONTROL on the floating-H0 machinery: theta_for(omega_c = 0.12, h = 0.674) reproduces the direct LCDM number to 1%   (theta_for = 1.03957 vs direct 1.03957)
  floating H0 with omega_c = 0: over h in [0.20, 2.00] the CLOSEST 100 theta_* to Planck is 0.96652 at h = 2.000, still 249 sigma away
  [PASS] P0-d  the geometric degeneracy does NOT rescue it: NO value of h in [0.20, 2.00] brings a no-CDM background back to Planck's theta_*.  The best is 0.96652 at h = 2.00, still 249 sigma out, and that h is itself excluded by the distance ladder.  Removing CDM breaks the CMB geometry outright   (best 100 theta_* at omega_c = 0 is 0.96652 at h = 2.00 (249 sigma); measured h = 0.674)

