  H_n = height of the n-th extremum of |Theta_0 + psi|^2 ; 'dmp' multiplies by exp(-2(k/k_D)^2).
  max|phi|/phi_p is the LARGEST the potential of the third-peak mode ever gets, in units of its primordial
  value.  In GR it never exceeds 1.  A value >> 1 means the run has left linear theory -- see P2-d.
  [PASS] P2-a  CONTROL restated as a target: deleting CDM drops the third-peak ratio H3/H1 from 1.6013 to 1.2761 (a factor 1.25), and the damped ratio from 0.6712 to 0.5497.  THAT is the deficit any replacement must make up   (H3/H1: LCDM 1.6013 -> no-CDM 1.2761 (factor 1.25 short))
  [PASS] P2-b  *** BRANCH A IS IRRELEVANT TO THE THIRD PEAK. ***  The boost a constant, dark-energy-scaled a0 applies to the third-peak mode at recombination is nu = 1.618 against the 6.36 an omega_c replacement needs.  It moves H3/H1 from 1.2761 to 1.2909, closing +5% of the gap when the boost is gated to sub-horizon and -13% when it is not -- i.e. the effect is at the few-per-cent level and its SIGN is not even robust to that choice.  A 62% force correction cannot substitute for a factor 6.4   (nu = 1.618 vs needed 6.36; H3/H1 1.2761 -> 1.2909 gated (+5% of the gap) / 1.2325 ungated (-13%); target 1.6013)
  [PASS] P2-c  *** BRANCH B IS EXCLUDED BY AMPLITUDE, NOT SHAPE. ***  With a0 propto H the deep-MOND boost acts throughout the radiation era and the perturbations RUN AWAY: the third-peak potential reaches max|phi|/phi_prim = 153 gated to sub-horizon (3.16e+04 ungated), against <= 1 in GR.  With phi_prim ~ 2e-5 that is |phi| ~ 0.0031 -- linear theory is gone and the predicted temperature anisotropy is orders above the measured 1e-5   (max|phi|/phi_p: branch B gated 153, ungated 3.16e+04; LCDM 1.000, no-CDM GR 1.000)
  [PASS] P2-d  quantified against the sky: the effective temperature |Theta_0 + psi| of the third-peak mode at last scattering is 3.6e-05 in LCDM and 0.0108 on branch B -- a factor 301 too large against a measured rms of ~1e-5.  The CMB does not need a peak-shape argument to exclude branch B; the ANISOTROPY AMPLITUDE does it   (|Theta_0+psi|(k3, z_rec): LCDM 3.602e-05, branch B 1.083e-02 (factor 301); observed rms ~ 1.1e-05)
  [PASS] P2-e  and the branch-B runaway SURVIVES the conservative horizon gate: restricting the boost to sub-horizon modes only (the only regime where a quasi-static MOND limit exists) changes max|phi|/phi_p from 3.16e+04 to 153 -- the kill is not an artefact of boosting super-horizon modes   (ungated 3.16e+04 vs gated 153)

======================================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE SIGN AND THE MECHANISM: does the boosted baryon potential stop decaying?
======================================================================================================================
  CDM's third-peak signature is that phi does NOT decay once matter dominates.  A boost multiplies phi;
  the question is whether nu(y) grows fast enough, and at the right time, to CANCEL the decay.
    mode k = 0.0653/Mpc (third peak).   phi(a)/phi_primordial along the integration:
