     1.589e-06   629453.4 |      0.9996      0.9999      0.9999   1.000       0.9999        1
     7.786e-06   128429.9 |      0.9968      0.9981      0.9981   1.000       0.9981        1
     2.565e-05    38988.6 |      0.9772      0.9802      0.9802   1.000       0.9802        1
     8.448e-05    11835.6 |      0.8293      0.8059      0.8061   1.001        31.14     5.67
     2.783e-04     3592.4 |      0.2740     -0.0035     -0.0028   1.016        147.7      2.5
     9.167e-04     1089.9 |      0.1698     -0.0091     -0.0092   1.492        27.16     3.63
  
  at recombination, |phi|/phi_prim : LCDM 0.16978   no-CDM GR 0.00911   (factor 19)
  at recombination, |psi_eff|/phi_p: no-CDM+A 0.01485 (nu = 1.618)   no-CDM+B 100.5 (nu = 3.7)
  [PASS] P3-a  THE MECHANISM IS NOT REPRODUCED.  In LCDM the third-peak potential survives at |phi|/phi_prim = 0.1698 because CDM stops the decay.  With no CDM it decays to 0.00911, a factor 19.  Branch A's boost lifts it only to 0.01485 -- still 11x short -- and does so at the END, which is a different time dependence and therefore a different driving history, not a reproduction of the mechanism   (|phi|/phi_p at z_rec: LCDM 0.1698, no-CDM 0.00911, no-CDM+A(psi) 0.01485)
  [PASS] P3-b  and the two are NOT degenerate even where the endpoint amplitudes could be matched: a potential that never decayed and a potential that decayed and was multiplied up drive the oscillator differently, because the driving is the integral of psi over the whole history.  Branch B demonstrates it by overshooting the LCDM endpoint by 592x while having decayed through the radiation era   (|psi|/phi_p at z_rec: LCDM(GR) 0.1698, no-CDM+B 100.5)

======================================================================================================================
PART 4 -- THE NODE PATHOLOGY: a MOND boost on an OSCILLATING source
======================================================================================================================
  nu(y) = sqrt(1 + a0/g) is a DECREASING function of |g|.  An acoustic potential passes through zero twice
  per cycle, so the boost is LARGEST exactly where the potential is SMALLEST.  In deep MOND the driving
  term becomes k^2 psi = k^2 sign(phi) sqrt(a0 a |phi|/(k c^2)) -- proportional to sqrt(|phi|), not phi.
  A sublinear driving term pumps the TROUGHS rather than the crests and generates harmonics that are NOT
  at k r_s = n pi.  Both the singular (permode) and the regularised (envelope) evaluations are shown.
  no-CDM GR (reference)                        extrema at k r_s/pi = 0.895, 1.911, 2.927, 3.944
  branch A, permode  (node singularity live)   extrema at k r_s/pi = 0.895, 1.911, 2.927, 3.944
  branch A, envelope (singularity removed)     extrema at k r_s/pi = 0.895, 1.911, 2.927, 3.944
  branch B, permode  (node singularity live)   extrema at k r_s/pi = 0.526, 1.542, 2.558, 3.574
  branch B, envelope (singularity removed)     extrema at k r_s/pi = 0.526, 1.634, 2.650, 3.667
  LCDM GR (for comparison)                     extrema at k r_s/pi = 0.936, 1.894, 2.919, 3.945
  [PASS] P4-a  the DEEP-MOND (branch B) driving displaces the acoustic extrema relative to the SAME background without the boost by up to 41.3%, while branch A's weak boost displaces them by 0.00% (i.e. not at all).  Planck measures the peak spacing to 0.03%, so a displacement of this size is a   Planck measures the peak spacing to 0.03%, so branch B's displacement is a different spectrum, not a fitting nuisance -- and branch A's is nothing at all, which is the same verdict from the other side.  (Same-background comparison, so the r_s change from deleting CDM is not double-counted -- that was P0-b.)   (max fractional displacement of the first three extrema: branch B 41.28%, branch A 0.000%)
  [PASS] P4-b  and the pathology is NOT an artefact of the node singularity: the ENVELOPE evaluation, which removes the divergence entirely, is reported alongside and gives the same qualitative answer.  Verified both ways   (permode and envelope evaluations both run and both reported above)

======================================================================================================================
PART 5 -- HOW BIG A BOOST WOULD BE NEEDED, AND WHETHER nu CAN BE THAT SIZE AT THE RIGHT TIME
======================================================================================================================
  To make the baryons source the LCDM potential you need the gravitational source multiplied by (omega_b+omega_c)/omega_b = 6.36 -- and multiplied CONSTANTLY from before equality, not only at the end.
            z |  nu_A env  nu_A inst |   nu_B env  nu_B inst |  verdict vs the needed 6.36
      10000.0 |     1.001      1.001 |      4.834      6.336 |  A: NO (6.4x short)   B: yes
       5000.0 |     1.004      1.006 |      2.825       2.86 |  A: NO (6.3x short)   B: NO (2.3x short)
       3000.0 |     1.032      1.036 |      2.516      2.578 |  A: NO (6.2x short)   B: NO (2.5x short)
       2000.0 |     1.082      7.807 |        3.7       3.88 |  A: NO (5.9x short)   B: NO (1.7x short)
       1500.0 |     1.172      1.245 |      3.558       3.58 |  A: NO (5.4x short)   B: NO (1.8x short)
       1089.9 |     1.492      1.618 |      3.633      3.699 |  A: NO (4.3x short)   B: NO (1.8x short)
  'env' is the sustained boost (oscillator amplitude); 'inst' uses the instantaneous |phi| and therefore
  SPIKES wherever the acoustic potential crosses zero.  Those spikes last a negligible fraction of a cycle
  and are the node artefact of section 4, not a sustained enhancement -- both columns are shown so the
  difference cannot be hidden in either direction.
  [PASS] P5-a  BRANCH A never reaches the required factor 6.36 as a SUSTAINED boost at any pre-recombination epoch on the third-peak scale: its largest ENVELOPE boost over the whole history is nu = 1.492, a factor 4.3 short.  (Its instantaneous boost does momentarily reach 7.81, but only while the potential is crossing zero -- reported here explicitly rather than being quietly dropped, and it carries no time-integrated driving.)  A constant a0 tied to the dark-energy density cannot stand in for omega_c   (max sustained nu_A = 1.492 (instantaneous node spike 7.81), needed 6.36)
  [PASS] P5-b  BRANCH B overshoots and, worse, its overshoot is TIME-DEPENDENT in the wrong direction: it is a runaway, not a rescaling.  A source term that grows the potential by 153x cannot be traded against a constant factor 6.36   (max|phi|/phi_p on branch B = 153 vs the needed constant 6.36)

